{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KNUUUDn6RdSV45umVUe5Fc","type":"tool_result","content":"paper/sections/discussion.tex:12:Future work includes extending to additional model families and architectures, large-scale leaderboard audits pending estimation advances for RL-era models~\\citep{zhang2026rlvr}, and post-RL validation. The $\\ell_z^*$ statistic is structurally invariant to RL distributional changes; empirical verification is future work.\npaper/sections/limitations.tex:7:All controlled experiments target SFT-stage contamination. While $\\ell_z^*$ is structurally invariant to post-hoc distributional changes from reinforcement learning, empirical validation on post-RL models is deferred to future work.\npaper/sections/background.tex:41:{\\raggedright\\scriptsize $^{a}$\\citet{wang2025fragility}: 10 methods fail post-RL.\npaper/sections/introduction.tex:19:Binary response patterns are structurally invariant to RL-induced distributional changes, as they record what a model answered rather than how its internal distributions shifted (empirical verification on post-RL models is future work; see \\S\\ref{sec:discussion})."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01ShyAuzjZknBLj9G2fe8A2a","session_id":"44a048b4-6a0e-498e-861e-50d9d8212329","uuid":"92d60a18-fd5c-4a32-b780-49b137a6e29e","timestamp":"2026-05-21T05:37:39.795Z"}
